# Third-party coverage tools still emit these project-local trees. They are
# transient tool output, not Vrooli's governed Test Genie run store.
packages/*/coverage/
scenarios/*/ui/coverage/
templates/scenarios/*/ui/coverage/

# Playwright's project-local reporter output. Durable Test Genie evidence is
# copied into the contract-owned runtime store by the owning phase.
scenarios/*/test-results/

# protogen staging trees (packages/proto/protogen/generator.go). Generation
# stages a full copy of the generated fleet beside packages/proto and publishes
# from it; a failed run deliberately retains its tree for inspection. Retention
# is bounded by stageRetention, but the trees must never be commit candidates.
packages/.proto-gen-stage-*/
packages/.proto-gen-verify-*/
packages/.proto-descriptor-*/
*.lcov
**/coverage*.html
**/coverage*_report.*
**/coverage-report.*
**/TEST_COVERAGE_REPORT.*
**/coverage-detailed.*
**/coverage*.out
**/test-output*.txt
**/*test-output*.txt
**/test.bin
**/test-build
**/api/*-api
**/api/webconsole
# Ad-hoc Go build output. `go build` with no -o names the binary after its
# containing directory, so a bare `go build .` in api/ or cli/ drops an
# extensionless executable right next to the source. Every compiled binary that
# reached this repo's history arrived this way (never via the standard
# `go build -o "$(SCENARIO_NAME)-api"` above, which **/api/*-api already covers).
# gitignore cannot express "extensionless executable", so these patterns cover
# only the predictable shapes; `vrooli hygiene` owns the general backstop via its
# tracked_binaries check.
scenarios/*/api/api
scenarios/*/api/main
scenarios/*/cli/cli
scenarios/*/cli/main
resources/*/api/api
resources/*/api/main
resources/*/cli/main
# Build-freshness manifests: regenerable, host-specific cache stamped next to
# each build artifact (mtime/toolchain-keyed, self-healing). Never committed.
**/*.freshness.json
bin/
.vrooli/*-agents.json
.vrooli/*.lock
.vrooli/browserless/
.vrooli/running-resources.json
.vrooli/schemas/resource-definitions.json

